sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — MorphoEval overall 70.6/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "The script is a serious, well-instrumented implementation of the Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) orientation- hypercolumn model: the local/lateral Fourier-Bessel harmonics, the perturbative even/odd dispersion curves, the exact diagonalisation of the orientation operator (which genuinely derives the m=0 non-contoured vs m=1 contoured regime for the auto presets), the sigmoid-expansion weights, the eta-aware hexagon/roll thresholds and the two-regime log-polar map all check out against the papers as I know them, and the retinal pullbacks of the tunnel and the chiral, seamless spiral are convincing. Its weak points are structural rather than cosmetic: the \"full cubic\" quadratic-feedback path is a reconstruction that is unusable (subcritical / near-resonant) at every sigma0 != 1/2 in the very regime the gallery renders, the badged honeycomb is actually drawn with wavevectors at +-114.6 deg because of torus quantisation, the 1e-15 parity is with a Rust port rather than with any digitised paper figure, and the only empirical comparisons are the paper's own 30-36 stripe / 2.4-3.2 mm statements and Horton & Hoyt's magnification law, neither of which the parity presets meet (lambda_c 9.0 mm, 3.2x too long). Provenance (DOIs, PMIDs, SHA-256 pins, lock file, 40 passing self-test checks, no RNG) is strong, but the README section describing the script is stale relative to this Pass-4 code. Overall 70.6/100 (faithfulness 66.0, reproducibility 81.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 2aac102; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 74, Morphological realism / specimen match 66, Parameter expressivity 62, Morphometric validation 58, Source and data traceability 84, Code-to-model traceability 74, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at 2aac102, image/png, 1852599 B, 3577×2495 px, artifact_sha256 59ee2445fa3cc7fe6fa27a91b99eb16d2b412d31933f5869271e80c9a736ef7c (sha256 59ee2445fa3cc7fe6fa27a91b99eb16d2b412d31933f5869271e80c9a736ef7c), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; artifact_sha256: 59ee2445fa3cc7fe6fa27a91b99eb16d2b412d31933f5869271e80c9a736ef7c; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bressloff/driven-neural-fields-registry.json=4f07b5175a48bcb5..., datasets/bressloff/paper-calibration.json=af12b2c1aa3e38fa..., datasets/bressloff/rule-2011-floquet.json=5e349c7b80185de4...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Bressloff et al. (2001, 2002): a Euclidean shift-twist symmetric neural field on the orientation-hypercolumn lattice of V1 undergoes a Turing-type instability whose even/odd, contoured (m=1) / non-contoured (m=0) planforms, pulled back through the retino-cortical map (2001 Section 2: x=(alpha/eps)ln(1+eps r/w0), y=beta theta/eps; 2002 Eq. 1.1: y=beta r theta/(w0+eps r)), give Klüver's four form constants; cubic amplitude equations (2001 Eqs. 5.9-5.15) with coefficients built from the firing-rate derivatives sigma_2, sigma_3 and a quadratic-feedback term select rolls, rhombi, squares or hexagons; the 2002 paper states a foveal magnification of 11.5 mm/deg, 30-36 perceived stripes and a cortical wavelength of 2.4-3.2 mm | Ermentrout & Cowan (1979): cortical rolls map to tunnels, funnels and spirals under the log-polar retino-cortical map (the non-contoured limit) | Horton & Hoyt (1991): human V1 linear cortical magnification follows M(E) = 17.3/(E + 0.75) mm/deg | Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout (2011): periodic flicker drives 1:1 (stripe) and 2:1 period-doubling (hexagon) Floquet resonance tongues over forcing period and wave number | Tamekue, Prandi & Chitour (2024): a Gaussian-only (no Mexican-hat) lateral kernel produces no MacKay-type pattern, used here as the negative control; reconstructed_in_script: Perturbative Fourier-Bessel even/odd dispersion scans with exact parity to the upstream fixture (5 stability_reports, 24 preset runs, all 133 paper-expectation checks counted, 121 pass) kept as branch_selection_upstream; PLUS the exact Hermitian orientation-space operator on e^{2 i m phi}, |m| <= 8, diagonalised directly (top eigenvalue within 3e-4 of the perturbative scan, dq* = 0) whose dominant harmonic derives the contoured/non-contoured regime (switch at local inhibition A_loc ~ 0.24-0.25 where W0 = W1); fixture presets that impose a non-critical harmonic or parity are flagged (imposed_harmonic, parity_imposed_subcritical) | Full cubic amplitude coefficients gamma(theta) = [3 s3 Gamma_3 - 2 s2^2 Q]/N with sigmoid derivative weights s2 = (1-2 sigma0)/2, s3 = (6 sigma0(1-sigma0)-1)/6 and the quadratic feedback Q through the resolvent (lambda_c - W_K)^-1 W_K at K = 0 and K = k_i +/- k_j (critical direction removed); eta = 2 s2 Gamma_2 / N with the eta-aware thresholds Lambda_r < Lambda_h; roll stability tested against every perturbation direction theta on a 5-degree grid, squares/rhombi against all external directions; at sigma0 = 1/2 the coefficients reduce to the upstream bare overlaps (gamma(60)/gamma(0) 0.4864 vs 0.4870); a feedback_fraction > 1 flag (near_resonant) and a gamma(0) <= 0 flag (subcritical) mark where the cubic truncation is unreliable; a regime map over A_loc x sigma0 (260 cells) and sweeps over lateral width, lateral inhibition, lateral spread, local inhibition and sigma0 | Gallery of five planforms rendered at each branch's own q* with k_x and k_y quantised to integer torus cycles: derived non-contoured tunnel and spiral (SELECTED: rolls stable with min 2 gamma/gamma0 - 1 = +0.92), contoured cobweb (IMPOSED-unstable), honeycomb (STABLE-coexisting) and the selected rhombic lattice; contoured planforms use the signed envelope with the exact eigenfunction u(phi) and an orientation field drawn as line elements in cortex and, via the tangent map phi_R = phi + theta_R, in the visual field | Retinal pullback through the conformal complex-log angular coordinate by default (cortical torus closes exactly: seam 0.00, spiral chirality 0.89 with the LR/UD reflection metric) with the exact 2002 coordinate retained (--retinal-map exact) and its seams quantified on all four half-meridians under full-field, chiral-mirror and bilateral-mirror conventions; retinal morphometrics (ring counts fovea to 90 degrees on the model map and the Horton-Hoyt map, spoke count, cortical roll angle vs visual log-spiral angle) | A paper_scale_tunnel preset (lateral widths / 3.3, q scan to 6): q* = 4.84, lambda_c = 2.60 mm (paper 2.4-3.2), 29 rings fovea to 90 degrees on the alpha = 3/pi map vs 32 on the Horton-Hoyt map (paper 30-36); comparison of the map's magnification with Horton & Hoyt (1991) (RMS 6.8%) and with the 2002 paper's own scale anchors; a Gaussian-only negative control cross-referenced to the vendored registry; and a diagnostic overlay of the Rule (2011) tongue boundaries (16 curves over 5 forcing amplitudes) with its calibration status printed; transfer_boundary: Numerical parity to 2.2e-16 is with the MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants Rust implementation's stability_reports and runs, not with digitised figures of the 2001 paper; alpha = 3/pi and beta = 1.589/2 are the upstream params.rs values; the parity presets' rendered wavelength 8.7 mm is 3.1x the paper's and the paper-scale preset is a repo-added parameter choice (lateral widths / 3.3) that reaches the paper's wavelength but not the paper's parameter values | The quadratic-feedback term is evaluated through the linear resolvent of the same flat-dispersion operator, whose uniform K = 0 mode is nearly marginal; for sigma0 != 1/2 the feedback dominates the bare cubic term (resolvent gain 50-2000) and the script flags these cells near_resonant instead of reporting a selection (178 of 260 regime-map cells are subcritical or feedback-dominated) — a mean-mode-coupled amplitude equation (Matthews & Cox 2000) would be needed there | In the contoured (m = 1) regime rolls and squares are unstable for every sigma0 and the cobweb remains an imposed lattice; the non-contoured regime in which tunnels and spirals are SELECTED is reached by lowering the local inhibition to A_loc = 0.15 (a repo-added preset), not by the fixture's parameters | The conformal angular map removes the pullback seam by construction (the torus closes exactly); the exact 2002 map's seams (left meridian 11.0 full-field; vertical meridians 10.3 chiral-mirror) are quantified, not fixed, because that map cannot close the torus at finite r; does_not_claim: Fifth-order (quintic) resolution of the odd-branch hexagon/triangle degeneracy or of the subcritical sigma0 <= 0.25 cases (Bressloff 2001 Section 5), a mean-mode-coupled amplitude equation for the near-resonant K = 0 mode, a Floquet solver or validated reproduction of Rule (2011) Fig. 8 (the vendored fixture is marked diagnostic-only upstream and the script says so), a derivation of the paper's parameter values from first principles, or a comparison with subject drawings of hallucinations." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:1280-1283: with eta = 0 at sigma0 = 1/2 the honeycomb's 'STABLE, coexists' badge rests on d_h/gamma0 = 2*gamma(60)/gamma0 - 1 = -0.0083, i.e. a 0.8% margin from the exactly-marginal pure- cos(2 phi) value 1/2, on a 5-deg theta grid with 720 phi samples and interpolated shifts; print the margin on the badge and test its sensitivity to ORIENT_SAMPLES/ORIENT_HARMONICS before calling the hexagon stable.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:1603-1616 (claim at 1568-1572): k_y quantisation to integer torus cycles turns the fig35_hex_zero_even wavevectors into (0, +-114.62 deg) with n_y = 10 of 11 cycles — a 5.4 deg distortion, not '< 1 degree' — so the panel badged 'STABLE, coexists' as a 60-deg hexagon renders a 65/115-deg lattice; pick n or the cycle count so 11*sin(60) is near-integer, or quantise |k| and angle jointly and print the realised angles on the panel.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:2429: comment reads 'lateral widths /3.1 so q* ~ 4.5 and lambda_c ~ 2.8 mm' but the paper_scale_tunnel preset (588-592) divides by 3.3 and yields q* = 4.84, lambda_c = 2.60 mm; align the comment with the preset.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:2642 (and 1457): the kluver_form_constant CSV rows write stab['critical_q'] = 1.491139 (the perturbative n=1-anchored scan) under the column 'critical_q' for the two m=0 panels that are rendered at q_mode = 1.403797; write q_mode (or add a column) so the CSV's q* matches the rendered wavelength 8.95 mm.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:3202-3203: the ledger line is hard-coded to say '=> 2k harmonic of tanh o max' while the values it prints for the hex panel (power at k/sqrt3k/2k = 0.97/1.00/0.17) show the sqrt(3)k difference ring dominating; derive the label from argmax of the three powers (the self-test at 3697-3702 already accepts either).",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:796-817 and 988-992: the quadratic-feedback coefficient gamma = [3 s3 Gamma3 - 2 s2^2 Q]/N with Q = <u0^2 R_0[u_th^2]> + <u0 u_th (R_+ + R_-)[u0 u_th]> is introduced as 'derived here for the operator as implemented'; no equation number of Bressloff 2001 section 5 is cited for the prefactors or for the K = 0 / K = k_i +- k_j decomposition, and no digitised Fig. 37-40 value is compared — add the paper's expression (or an appendix derivation) and at least one numeric check against the published coefficient curves rather than only against the Rust port.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:947-1008 with 2221/2478: in the derived m=0 regime the full-cubic path is subcritical and near-resonant at every sigma0 != 0.5 (my `--sweep sigmoid_baseline:0.3:0.7:5 --preset roll_noncontoured_derived` gave roll margins -105..-117 and 'hexagonal SUBCRITICAL' at 4/5 points; resonance_gap 0.019), so the sigma0 parameter and the quadratic-feedback machinery contribute nothing testable where the gallery lives; either implement the Matthews-Cox mean-mode coupling or restrict the sigma0 sweep/regime map to the reliable window and state that in Panel B/G titles.",
            "remediation needed: README.md:433-441: the author's section is stale relative to Pass 4 — it says `--preset ID` 'select[s] what is rendered' (it only seeds `--sweep`, script 3780/3819), lists `--hemifield-mode {full-field,bilateral-mirror}` (chiral-mirror missing), claims '27 checks in ~12 s' (40 checks, 75 s here), badges tunnel/spiral/cobweb as IMPOSED (now SELECTED/SELECTED/IMPOSED) and quotes lambda_c 8.7 mm for the gallery (now 9.0 mm for the derived presets).",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:2480-2496 — `sweep_summary` (and the `parameter_sweep` CSV rows at `lines 2807-2828` plus `kluver_form_constant` CSV rows at `line 2643`) aggregates `q_star_min`, `q_star_max`, and `parity_flips` from the perturbative `n=1` fields (`critical_q`, `critical_branch`) rather than `critical_q_exact` / `q_mode` and `critical_parity_exact`, causing `bressloff_v1_metrics.csv:55` to report two false parity flips at `A_loc = 0.225, 0.25` and a false `q*_min = 0.729134` from the `O(beta^2)` zero-denominator singularity at `W_1^loc = W_0^loc`, and logging `critical_q = 1.491139` instead of `1.403797` for the `m=0` gallery presets (`bressloff_v1_metrics.csv:31-32,56`).",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:2686 — In the `cubic_coefficients_full` CSV writer, `'bare gamma3/N @ same'` is computed as `3.0 * bs['s3'] * v / bs['gamma0']`, omitting the `1 / N` (`N = <u_0^2>`) factor present in `bs['gamma0']` (`line 992`); for all `m=1` gallery presets (`N ~ 0.5`), the exported bare ratios in `bressloff_v1_metrics.csv:38-40` (`0.500, 0.416, 0.248...`) are halved relative to `gamma(theta)/gamma(0)` (`1.000, 0.832, 0.496...`) at `sigma0 = 0.5`.",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:2933-2952 — Panel A defines `stab_gal = rendered_gallery[0]['stability']` (which is `roll_noncontoured_derived` at `A_loc = 0.15`, where `n=1` perturbation theory is invalid because `W_1^loc < W_0^loc`) and plots `stab_gal['even_growth']` (`q* = 1.49`) under the label `'Gallery presets even (theta_0=60 deg, xi_hat_lat=1.5, q*=1.49)'`, misrepresenting the contoured `A_loc = 1.0` gallery presets in Columns III-V (`q* = 1.45`).",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:3361-3390 — `make_gif` passes `envelope_only=True` (`line 3362`) and hardcodes `'non-contoured'` in `fig.suptitle` (`line 3389`) for all five gallery presets, stripping the contoured `argmax_phi` envelope and orientation line elements from Columns 3-5 (`fig31_square_even`, `fig35_hex_zero_even`, `fig33_rhombic_even`) and mislabeling them as non-contoured in `docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif`.",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:855 — `exact_orientation_modes` computes the dominant harmonic via `dom = int(abs(_HARM_M[int(np.argmax(np.abs(v)))]))` on complex exponential coefficients `e^{2im*phi}` instead of combining conjugate pairs into the real harmonic L2 norm `sqrt(|v_+m|^2 + |v_-m|^2) = sqrt(2)*|v_m|` for `m >= 1`; this biases the m=0 vs m=1 classification by sqrt(2), misclassifies modes with up to 66.7% m=1 power (e.g. A_loc=0.24-0.25) as `harmonic=0`, shifts the reported full-operator harmonic flip to `A_loc=0.275` (`bressloff_v1_metrics.csv:47`), and leaves `exact_curves['even_1']` as `NaN` at 118/128 wavenumbers at `A_loc=0.24`.",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:926-937 — `resolvent_apply` projects out the critical eigenspace only when `abs(lam_c - vals[i]) < 1.0e-6 * max(abs(lam_c), 1e-12)`, which removes the `|k_1 - k_2| = q*` triad resonance at `theta = 60 deg` (`Q(60 deg) = 0.3170`) but leaves an unprojected near- resonant pole on the critical branch at adjacent grid angles `theta = 55 deg` (`Q = 0.6991`) and `theta = 65 deg` (`Q = 0.8307`), creating artificial spikes in Panel B for `sigma0 != 0.5` and shifting `rhombic_theta_optimal_deg` from `45 deg` to `55 deg` at `sigma0 = 0.4` (`2001-bressloff-v1-form- constants.py:3598-3601`).",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] README.md:435-458 — The top-level `README.md` section `### [2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py]` is stale from Pass 3: it states that tunnel and spiral are badged `IMPOSED: unstable`, that the cubic coefficients are bare overlaps without `sigma0` weights or quadratic feedback, that no swept parameter changes the selected family, that the default pullback has a 7-10x left- meridian seam, and that `--self-test` runs 27 checks in ~12 s, contradicting the Pass 4 code and outputs." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.706"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

